00:16:31.310 --> 00:16:33.260
App Script is Google's
scripting language that

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:37.460
is a subset of ES5 JavaScript.

00:16:37.460 --> 00:16:39.980
You can code on the
web UI, or you can also

00:16:39.980 --> 00:16:43.190
code locally and push
the code into the web UI.

00:16:43.190 --> 00:16:46.040
It works very well with
other Google technologies

00:16:46.040 --> 00:16:49.550
like Docs, Sheets,
Slides, and Google APIs,

00:16:49.550 --> 00:16:51.200
and services like Big Query.

00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:52.116
FELIPE HOFFA: Exactly.

00:16:52.116 --> 00:16:54.980
So with a few lines
of code, I can get

00:16:54.980 --> 00:16:56.720
App Script to query Big Query.

00:16:56.720 --> 00:16:59.000
And with no code, I
can schedule App Script

00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:03.015
to go there every hour, every
day, whenever I want to run it.

00:17:03.015 --> 00:17:03.890
MINHAZ KAZI: Awesome.

00:17:03.890 --> 00:17:06.180
So what do you do with
this App Script thing?

00:17:06.180 --> 00:17:09.260
FELIPE HOFFA: [INAUDIBLE] I
scheduled it to work every hour

00:17:09.260 --> 00:17:11.160
and I added three lines of code.

00:17:11.160 --> 00:17:14.810
So App Script would materialize
the results of my query

00:17:14.810 --> 00:17:16.280
into Google Cloud Storage.

00:17:16.280 --> 00:17:19.010
This is all it takes to
materialize to Google Cloud

00:17:19.010 --> 00:17:19.920
